        # ReleaseNotes of this module
        ReleaseNotes = 'What''s New in v1.0.28

Full release notes: https://github.com/jullienl/HPE-COM-PowerShell-Library/releases/tag/v1.0.28



BUG FIXES

- Fixed a crash of the PowerShell session when an automatic session renewal was rejected: the renewal now stops after a few attempts and asks you to reconnect.
- Connect-HPEGL -Workspace now connects to newly created workspaces, which could fail with "Workspace not found or not accessible" for some time after creation.
- Clearer error when signed in without a workspace selected: commands now explain how to connect to a workspace instead of reporting that no session was found.
- Get-HPEGLDeviceAutoSubscription now displays a warning when no auto-subscription settings are configured, instead of returning nothing.
- "Unauthorized" errors from HPE GreenLake now explain the likely causes and how to reconnect.
- Get-HPECOMJob -JobResourceUri (or piped job objects) no longer displays a misleading "MetadataError ... not a valid value for the Name variable" error.
- Remove-HPEGLWorkspace no longer wrongly warns that the organization will be deleted when removing its last member workspace.



IMPROVEMENTS

- New-HPEGLWorkspace -InOrganization creates the workspace as a member of the current organization (previously, workspaces were always created as standalone workspaces). New -Description parameter.

